      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0071_seg_002"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "1) There is currently no provision for 6MB PICs. Designers of 8 MB memory boards should consider auto-configs as two PICs to allow partial loading flexibility.\n\n2) PIC size/alignment rules are subject to change. If so, bit(s) will be defined to allow a PIC to specify that it is more flexible than the old rules require.\n\n3) The address map is subject to change. A PIC should assume that it may be placed anywhere in the address space.\n\n4) All expansion devices are strongly encouraged to use the auto-config protocols. Assignment of fixed I/O addresses is subject to negotiation.",
      "bbox": [
        816,
        596,
        2070,
        1220
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0071_seg_003"
    },
    {
